            "Trigonal system for the host quartz; inclusions keep their own system. No cleavage; conchoidal fracture. Hardness 7; specific gravity 2.65 on average, higher depending on the amount of inclusions; vitreous lustre; transparent to translucent; refractive index 1.544 to 1.553. Inclusions can create internal stress; enhydro quartz must not be heated or cut too close to the bubble. They are cut as cabochons, spheres, polished points and faceted stones that show off the inner “landscape”.",
            "Brazil: Minas Gerais and Bahia, rutilated, chlorite, phantom and variously included quartz. Madagascar: quartz with chlorite, rutile and hematite inclusions. United States: Arkansas (Hot Springs, Mount Ida), phantom and chlorite-included crystals. Also Colombia (multi-inclusion quartz), Pakistan, Switzerland and France (Alpine clefts of the Mont Blanc massif), China and India.",
            "A stone of self-knowledge and revelation, said to amplify the effect of the included minerals and help see beyond appearances; phantoms are associated with personal growth. It is associated with the crown chakra and all signs. Cleanse with water or smudging; recharge in gentle sunlight or moonlight."
